Jesus' family.
This is the genealogical record of Jesus Christ. He is the son of David. He is also the son of Abraham.
Abraham begat Isaac. Isaac begat Jacob. Jacob begat Judah and his brothers.
Judah fathered Perez and Zerah. Their mother was Tamar. Perez fathered Hezron. Hezron fathered Ram.
Ram was the father of Amminadab. Amminadab was the father of Nahshon. Nahshon was the father of Salmon.
Salmon was the father of Boaz. Rahab was the mother of Boaz. Boaz was the father of Obed. Ruth was the mother of Obed. Obed was the father of Jesse.
And Jesse was the father of King David. David was the father of Solomon. Solomon's mother was the wife of Uriah.
Solomon was the father of Rehoboam. Rehoboam was the father of Abijah. Abijah was the father of Asa.
Asa the son of Yehoshafat. Yehoshafat the son of Yohoram. Yohoram the son of Ahaziah.
Uzziah is the father of Jotham. Jotham is the father of Ahaz. Ahaz is the father of Hezekiah.
Hezekiah the father of Menahem. Menahem the father of Amnon. Amnon the father of Joash.
And Josiah begat Jeconiah and his brethren, in the days of Josiah his father, in the land of Judah. And in that same year came Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon unto Jerusalem, and besieged it. And the Lord sent unto Hezekiah king of Judah, saying, And now, I pray thee, consider how this great thing is come to pass, that the king of Babylon should come and smite this land, and destroy it. And Hezekiah king of Judah sent to Babylon to Babylon, saying, The great god of the kings of Judah hath sent to know of thee, because a great quaking was in Jerusalem, so that the people fled to me, saying, The god of this place is God of all the earth, and he will turn away the face of the mighty men of Egypt, so that they shall be consumed, as every man of Israel was consumed by whom he was consumed. And now, I pray thee, let there be a true testimony, that I have made a covenant with the Lord God of Israel, that he may confirm his great promise, which he promised to our fathers, to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob. And I have made a covenant with the house of Israel, and with the house of Judah, that they might execute all the commandments which the Lord commanded by the hand of Moses. And the Lord God of Israel made a covenant with the house of Israel, and with the house of Judah, in the land of Jerusalem. And the Lord God of Israel spake unto the children of Israel, saying, Take these words, and lay them up in the ark of the covenant of the Lord your God, that it may remain there for ever. And the children of Israel did so, and took great stones, and laid them up in the ark of the covenant of the Lord, and they remained there for ever. And the Lord said unto Moses, Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When ye be come into the land which I give unto you, and when ye shall rest every man under his vine and under his fig tree, then shall it be, that when any man shall hear the sound of a trumpet, and see the sword, and the drawn sword, and the hoofs of horses, and the chariots going to and fro, then shall he go into the inner house, and shut the door about him, and hold the door fast, and the sound of the trumpet shall not cease, but the sound of the trumpet shall be continual, and the people shall not go out into the field, nor thrust in their sick into the house of Israel. And the Lord said unto Moses, Write for thyself these words, for in very deed, I will drive out before thee the Amorites, and the Canaanites, and the Hittites, and the Perizzites, and the Jebusites; and I will deliver them up before thee, and thou shalt do unto them according to the commandments which I have given thee. And ye shall destroy utterly all that stood before you, and utterly destroy their cities, and their houses, and their lands, and their vineyards, and their olive trees, and whatsoever of their own do they stand before you; and destroy them utterly as I commanded you. And make no covenant with them, nor show mercy unto them; neither shalt thou make marriage with them; thy daughter thou shalt not give for his son, nor for his daughter shalt thou take his son, or his daughter shalt thou take, to go in unto them; this is your abomination which I hate. Do all these words, which I command thee, both to the kings of these nations which are round about you, and to the people which dwell in this wood; and cut them out, and destroy them utterly after that ye have read the words of this covenant, which all the people of the land are commanded to obey. And bind these words for a sign upon your hand, that they may be a token upon your hand, and a memorial between your eyes, that you may give instruction to your son, and to your son's son, to observe to do all the words of this law, which the Lord commanded Moses to give to the children of Israel, to all the words of this law, which the Lord
From that time, the family line continued. Jeconiah was the father of Shealtiel. Shealtiel was the father of Zerubbabel.
Zerubbabel was the father of Abiud. Abiud was the father of Eliakim. Eliakim was the father of Azor.
Azur was the father of Sadok. Sadok was the father of Achem. Achem was the father of Elias.
Eliud was the father of Eleazar. Eleazar was the father of Matan. Matan was the father of Jacob.
Jacob was the father of Joseph. Joseph was the husband of Mary. And Mary gave birth to Jesus, who is called the Christ.
There were 14 generations from Abraham to David. There were 14 from David until the Jewish people were forced to go to Babylon. And there were 14 from that time to Christ. Jesus Christ was born
Thus was the birth of Jesus Christ. His mother was Mary and Joseph had promised to marry her. But before they began to live together, it became clear that she was pregnant. She conceived through the power of the Holy Spirit.
Her husband Youssef was a righteous man. He did not want to let her be ashamed in public. So he planned to divorce her freely.
But when Joseph thought about this, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream. The angel said, "Joseph, son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary into your home as your wife. For the child within her was conceived by the Holy Spirit."
She is going to give birth to a son. You must name him Jesus. This is because he will save his people from their sins.
All of this happened so that what our Lord said would happen. He said it through the Prophet,
The virgin will conceive a son. She will find a boy. And they will name him Emmanuel. The name Emmanuel means "God is with us".
Joseph awoke. He did what the angel of the Lord commanded him. He took Mary into his house as his wife.
But he didn't do it even after she gave birth to a son. And Joseph called him Jesus.
The wise men visit Jesus.
Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judea. This took place when Herod was king of Judea. After Jesus was born, wise men from the east came to Jerusalem.
They asked, "Who is the child who was born king of the Jews? When we were in the East, we saw his star. Now we have come to worship him."
When King Herod heard this, he was deeply disturbed, and all the people of Jerusalem were also disturbed.
Herod called together all the chief priests of the people, as well as the teachers of the law. He asked them where the Messiah would be born.
"In Bethlehem of Judea," they said, "this is what the prophet wrote: 'The Lord God announced to King David, your ancestor: "Because your son, Solomon, is dedicated to me as king, I will ensure his kingdom will always be under the control of my son, the one who comes from my essence. I will always be his God, and he will always be my son."' "
But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah, though you are small among the clans of Judah, yet out of you shall come one who will be a ruler of Israel, whose origin is from old, from ancient times.
Then Herod secretly called the Magi. He learned from them the exact time when the star appeared.
Let them go to Bethlehem. He said, "Go! Get accurate information about the child. As soon as you find him, give me a report. Then we will go and worship him too."
After the wise men heard the word from the king, they went on their way. The star that they had seen when they were in the east, went before them. It finally stood over the place where the child was.
When they saw the star, they were filled with joy.
The wise men went to the house. There they saw the child with his mother Mary. They entered and prostrated themselves to him. Afterwards they opened their treasures. They gave him gold, frankincense, and myrrh.
But God warned them in a dream not to return to Herod. So they returned to their country by another way. Jesus' family flees to Egypt
When the wise men were gone, Joseph had a dream. In the dream, an angel of the Lord appeared to him. "Get up!" the angel said. "Take the child and his mother and flee to Egypt. Stay there until I tell you to return. Herod is going to search for the child. He wants to kill him."
Joseph got up. During the night, he left for Egypt with the child and his mother Mary.
They remained there until King Herod died. In this way, the word of the Lord spoken through the prophet was fulfilled: "In the land of Egypt I will again make you live in the presence of Pharaoh. Therefore, says the Lord God, I will now stretch out my hand, that I may strike down those who dwell in this land, from the least to the greatest." (Ezekiel 11:1)
Herod understood that the wise men had deceived him. He became very angry. He issued orders regarding Bethlehem and the surrounding area. All the boys who were two years old and under were to be killed. This corresponded to the time that the wise men had seen the star.
Therefore, the words of the prophet Jeremiah, which he spoke, were fulfilled. He said:
A voice was heard in Ramah. It was the voice of weeping and deep sorrow. Rachel wept for her children. She would not be comforted, because they were gone. The return of Jesus' family to Nazareth.
After Herod died, Joseph had a dream while still in Egypt. In the dream, an angel of the Lord appeared to him.
The angel said, "Arise! Take the child and his mother, and go to the land of Israel. Those who were trying to kill the child are dead."
Then Joseph awoke. He took the child and his mother Mary, returning to the land of Israel.
But after he heard that Archelaus was reigning over Judea. Archelaus was ruling in place of his father Herod. This frightened Justin from coming there. After he was warned in a dream, Justin returned to the land of Galilee instead.
He lived in a city called Nazareth. Thus, what the prophets had said about Jesus was fulfilled. They had said, "He will be called a Nazarene."
John the Baptist is preparing the way.
In those days John the Baptist came preaching in the wilderness of Judea.
He said, "Repent of your sins! The Kingdom of Heaven is at hand."
John is the one about whom the prophet Isaiah spoke, saying: "A voice cries out in the wilderness: 'Prepare the way for the Lord, make his paths straight.'" (Isaiah 40:3)
John was wearing clothes made of camel hair. He had a leather belt around his waist. His food was locusts and wild honey.
People went out to him from Jerusalem and all Judea. They came from the entire region around the Jordan River.
When they confessed their sins, John baptized them in the Jordan River.
John the Baptist, whom many Pharisees and Sadducees were coming to see where he was baptizing, said to them, "You brood of vipers! Who warned you to flee from the wrath to come?"
Produce fruit that shows you have repented of your sins.
What I want you to think about yourselves is, 'Abraham is our father.' I tell you, God is able to raise children even from these stones.
The vine is planted at the roots of the trees. Every tree that does not bear good fruit will be cut down. You will gather them and throw them into the fire.
I baptize you with water, calling you to repent of your sins. But after me, one will come who is mightier than I. I am not worthy to carry his sandals. He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit and fire.
His problem is in his hand to purify the straw from his yard. He will gather his wheat to the granary. But he will burn the chaff with an unquenchable fire". Jesus was baptized
Jesus came from Galilee to the Jordan River. He wanted to be baptized by John.
But John tried to prevent him. He said to Jesus, "I need to be baptized by you. So why have you come to me?"
Then Jesus answered: "Let us be thus for now. It is true we must do thus. It fulfills God's holy plan." Then John agreed.
From the time Jesus sneezed, he arose from the water. At that moment the heavens of the individual opened. Jesus saw the Spirit of God descending upon him like a dove.
A voice from heaven said, "This is my son, whom I love. I am very pleased with him."
Jesus is a laboratory.
The Holy Spirit entered Jesus into the desert. There the devil tempted him.
After 40 days and 40 nights of fasting, Jesus was hungry.
The experimenter came to him and said, "If you are the Son of God, command this stone to become bread."
Jesus answered, "It is written, 'Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceeds from the mouth of God.'" (Deuteronomy 8:3)
Then the devil took Jesus to the holy city. He directed him to stand on the highest point of the temple.
So if you are the Son of God, he said, cast yourself down, for it is written: "He will command his angels concerning you, and they will lift you up in their hands, so that you will not strike your foot against a stone." (Psalm 91:11, 12)
Jesus answered and said to him, "It is written, 'You shall not tempt the Lord your God.'" (Deuteronomy 6:16)
Finally, the devil took Jesus to a very high mountain. He showed him all the kingdoms of the world and their glory.
If you kneel down to me and worship me, he said, that's all I've given you.
Jesus said to him, "Get behind me, Satan! For it is written, 'Worship the Lord your God, and serve him only.'" (Deuteronomy 6:13)
Then the devil left Jesus. Angels came and provided him with care. Jesus began to preach.
John was put in prison. When Jesus heard about this, he returned to Galilee.
Jesus left Nazareth and moved to live in the town of Capernaum. It was by the lake in the region of Zebulun and Naphtali.
Therefore, what the prophet Isaiah said came true. He said,
Land of Zebulun! Land of Naphtali! Galilee, where non-Jewish people live! Land along the Mediterranean Sea! Lands east of the Jordan River!
The people who are living now in darkness will see a great light. They are living now in a very dark country. But a light will shine on them." (Isaiah 9:1,2)
From that time on, Jesus began to preach. "Repent of your sins," he said. "The Kingdom of Heaven is near." Jesus chooses the first disciples.
One day Jesus was walking by the Sea of Galilee. There he saw two brothers. They were Simon Peter and his brother Andrew. They were casting a net into the lake. They were fishermen.
Come, follow me, said Jesus. "Here we will make you fishers of men."
Immediately, they emptied their nets and followed him.
Going from there, he saw two other brothers. They were James the son of Zebedee and his brother John. They were in a boat with their father Zebedee. And they were mending their nets, when Jesus called them.
Immediately they left the child and her father and followed Jesus. Jesus heals the sick.
Jesus went all over Galilee. There he taught in the synagogues. He preached the good news of God's kingdom. He saw all the sick and those who had any disease.
His news spread throughout all the lands of Syria. The people brought everyone who was sick with various diseases. Some were suffering agonizing death. Others were possessed by demons. Some were shaking with a strong desire. Others could not be freed. And their healing, Jesus healed every one of them.
Large crowds followed him. Some people came from Galilee, from the region known as the Decapolis, and from Jerusalem and Jericho. Others came from the region located across the Jordan River.
Jesus gives blessings.
Jesus saw the crowds. So he went up into a mountain and sat down. His disciples came to him.
From then on, he started teaching them. He said,
Blessed are those who hunger and thirst for righteousness. For theirs is the kingdom of heaven.
It is sad, congratulations to him. He will be condoled.
The blessed who have no pride. They are the ones who are going to take the earth.
Blessed are those who are persecuted and thirst for righteousness, for they will be satisfied.
The deceased who show mercy. They are the ones who show mercy.
Blessed are the pure in heart. They will see God.
Blessed are the peacemakers, for they will be called children of God.
Blessed are those who suffer for the sake of what is right. The kingdom of heaven belongs to them.
Blessed are you when people revile you and persecute you for my sake. Blessed are you too when people speak evil lies against me for your sakes.
My sister is happy and pleased. Your reward in Paradise is great. In the same way, people harmed those who were prophets a long time ago. Salt and light.
You are the salt of the earth. But what if the salt loses its taste? How can it be made salty again? It is no longer good for anything. It will be thrown out. People will walk over it.
You are the light of the world. A city on a hill cannot be hidden.
Also, people shouldn't put the light under the tagine. Instead, they should put it on a base. And after that, it will give light to all the people in the house.
You are the light of the world. A city set on a hill cannot be hidden. Let your light shine before others, so that they may see your good deeds and glorify your Father in heaven. Jesus gives the full meaning of the law.
Do not think that I have come to abolish the Law or the Prophets. I have not come to abolish them but to fulfill them. For truly, I say to you, until heaven and earth pass away, not the smallest letter or stroke of a pen will by any means disappear from the Law until everything is accomplished.
What I am going to tell you is the truth. Heaven and earth will pass away before a single letter or stroke disappears from the Law. Not the slightest stroke of the pen will disappear from the Law until all is accomplished.
Not one of the least important commandments was broken. Nor did you teach people to break them. If you had done this, you would have been the least important person in the Kingdom of Heaven. Instead, you practiced and taught these commandments. You will be an important person in the Kingdom of Heaven.
Here is what we say to you. You must be more righteous than the Pharisees and teachers of the law. If you are not, you will certainly not enter the kingdom of heaven. To murder
You have heard it said to those who were living before, "You shall not kill. (Exodus 20:13) Whoever kills will be judged."
But here is what I tell you. Do not be angry with your brother. Whoever is angry with his brother will be brought to judgment. Again, whoever says to his brother, 'Raca,' must be judged in the Sanhedrin. But whoever says, 'You fool!' will be in danger of the fire of hell.
Assume you are giving a gift at the altar. And you remember that your brother has something against you.
Leave your gift before the altar. First, go and reconcile with your brother. Then come and offer your gift.
Don't be afraid of someone who has a case against you and is threatening you with court. Settle things quickly. Be able to solve the problem with him, as you are still on the road together. Otherwise, he might hand you over to the arbitrator. The arbitrator might hand you over to the officer. And you might be sentenced and imprisoned in jail.
What I will tell you is the truth. You will not get out until you pay the last penny! Adultery
We have all heard it written, "You shall not commit adultery" (Exodus 20:14).
But here is what I am telling you. Do not even look at a woman the wrong way. Whoever does that has already committed adultery with her in his heart.
If your right eye causes you to stumble, tear it out and throw it away. For it is better for you to lose one part of your body than for your whole body to be thrown into hell.
If your right hand causes you to sin, cut it off and throw it away from you. Your hand is just one part of your body. It is better to lose it than to lose your whole body and enter hell. Divorce.
It was said, "If a man divorces his wife, he must give her a certificate of divorce" (Deuteronomy 24:1).
But here is what I say to you. Whoever divorces his wife causes her to commit adultery. And whoever marries the divorced woman commits adultery. A man may divorce his wife only if she has not been faithful to him. Faithfulness
Again, you have heard what was said to your people long ago. They were told, 'Do not break the promise you have given to the Lord your God. Keep the oath you swore to him.
But this is what I tell you. Do not seek any such promise ever. Do not seek it in the sky. This is the throne of God.
Do not make it in the earth's heaven. This is the seat of the man of God. Do not make it in Jerusalem's heaven. This is the city of the great King.
And don't swear by your head. You cannot make even a single white or black hair.
Let your yes be yes and your no be no. Anything more than this comes from the evil one. Be gentle with people.
You have heard it said, 'Eye for eye and tooth for tooth' (Exodus 21:24; Leviticus 24:20; Deuteronomy 19:21)
But this is what we tell you. Do not fight against an evil person. "If someone strikes you on your right cheek. Offer him your other cheek as well.
Suppose someone takes you to court to recover your shirt. Let him take his coat too.
Assume someone is forcing you to walk one mile. Walk two miles with him.
Give to whoever asks something of you. Don't answer whoever wants to borrow something from you. Love your enemy.
I had heard it said, 'Love your neighbor. (Leviticus 19:18) Hate your enemy.'
But that's what we tell you. Love your enemy. Pray for those who harm you.
From now on, be like your father in heaven. "He causes his sun to rise on the evil and the good, and sends rain on the righteous and the unrighteous."
If you love the one who loves you, what forms will you get? Even the stingy ones do this.
If you only greet your own people, what do you do more than others? Even depraved people do that.
Be perfect, therefore, as your heavenly Father is perfect.
A gift to people in need.
Be careful not to do righteous acts before people. Don't do them to show off to them. If you do them like this, your Father in heaven will not let you go unrewarded.
Wherever you were giving to those who needed, you did not publicize it with the sound of a trumpet. Do not be like those who create their own sport, boasting about what they have done in the synagogue and in the streets. They want people to be proud of them. What I am going to tell you is the truth. They have benefited from a full reward.
Do not say your left hand does not do what your right hand does when you give charity to those in need.
Then your giving will be done in secret. Your father will reward you. He sees what you do in secret. Prayer
While you are teaching, do not be like the people who deceive by claiming to be holy. They love to stand up and read in churches and on street corners. They love to appear pious to the people. What I am about to tell you is the truth. They have already received their full reward.
When you pray, go into your room. Close the door and pray to your Father who is unseen. He will reward you. Your Father sees what is done in secret.
Do not eat, talk more when you pray, this is something done by people who do not believe. They think he will hear them because they talk a lot.
Don't be like them. Your father knows what you need even before you ask him.
This is how you pray. "Our Father who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name.
Come, O King. May he do whatever you want to happen on earth, just as it is done in heaven.
Give us this day our daily bread.
Forgive us our trespasses, as we forgive those who trespass against us.
Save us from falling into sin when we are experimented with. Deliver us from evil.
Forgive people when they sin against you. If you do this, your Father in heaven will forgive you.
But if you do not forgive the sins of others, I do not want your Father to forgive your sins. Fasting.
And when you fast, do not look somber like the hypocrites, who make their faces look pale so that people will praise them for their fasting. I tell you the truth, they have already received the full reward for what they do.
But when you go away without eating, put olive oil on your head. Wash your face.
Then what people don't know is that you are fasting. Only your father who doesn't show up, he is the one who knows it. He rewards you. Your father sees what is done in secret. Store wealth in paradise.
Do not put money on the ground for yourselves. Rodents and rust can destroy it. Thieves can break in and steal it.
Be careful, store treasures for yourselves in heaven. There, no rodents or rust corrupt them. There, no thieves break in and steal them.
Your heart is where you are, your spoils are there.
The eye is like a lamp for the body. Let your eyes be filled. Thus your whole body will be filled with light.
But imagine if your eyes were poor. Thus your whole body would fill with darkness. If the light within you is darkness, then it is true darkness!
No one can serve two masters at the same time. Either he will hate one and love the other, or he will be devoted to one and despise the other. You cannot serve both God and money. So don't be worried.
Let me tell you, don't worry. Don't worry about your life and what you eat or drink. And don't worry about your body and what you wear. Isn't life greater than eating? Isn't the most important thing for the body more important than clothing?
Look at the birds in the sky. They do not sow or gather crops. They do not store crops in barns. Yet your heavenly Father feeds them. Are you not much more valuable than they?
Can't you add one more hour to your life by worrying?
Are you worried about clothing? Look at how wildflowers grow. They neither toil nor spin.
But that's what I'm telling you. Even Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like one of these flowers.
If God clothes wild plants with such magnificence, would it not be even better for you? Wild plants exist today, and tomorrow they are thrown into the fire. Your faith is very little!
Not a problem. Don't tell him, "What will we eat?" or "What will we drink?" or "What will we wear?"
People who don't have much religion follow all this stuff. Your father in heaven knows you need it.
But the most important thing is God's kingdom first. Do what He wants you to do. Then all these things will be added to you.
It's not a problem for tomorrow. Tomorrow will carry its own worries. Every day has its own problems.
Be just when you judge people.
Don't judge people. Because after you judge, you will be judged.
We judge you by what you judge people by. We measure you by what people are measured by.
You see a little mote of dust in your friend's eye, but you don't notice the wooden beam in your own eye.
How do you tell your friend, 'Let me take a twig out of your eye'? How do you say this when there is a piece of wood in your eye?
You fraud! First, take out your wooden eye from your eye socket. Then you will be able to see clearly to take out your friend's splinter from his eye.
Do not give what is sacred to dogs, and do not throw your pearls before swine. If you do this, they may trample them underfoot. After that, they may turn on you and tear you to pieces. Ask, seek, inquire.
He asked, and this is what he told you. Look, and this is what you will find. Knock, and this is what they will do for you.
Everyone who asks will receive. Whoever seeks finds. The door will be opened for the one who knocks.
Suppose your son asks for bread. If some of you give him a stone, what would you expect?
Or when will a fish ask? And if any of you gives him a serpent?
And if you are evil, you know how to give your children good gifts. So how much more will your Father in heaven give good gifts to those who ask him!
In everything, deal with people as you would have them deal with you. This is what is written in the Law and the Prophets. The great door and the small door.
Enter the Kingdom of God through the narrow gate. The gate is wide and the road is broad, leading to death and hell. Many people are walking on this road.
But the door is small and the path is narrow that leads to life. Few people find it. A tree and its fruit.
Beware of false prophets, which come to you in sheep's clothing, but inwardly they are ravening wolves.
Can we say what they are by their outward appearance from what they do. "Do people gather grapes from thorny bushes? Do they gather figs from thorny briers?
In the same way, every good tree produces good fruit. But a bad tree produces bad fruit.
A good tree does not bear bad fruit, and a bad tree does not bear good fruit.
Every tree that does not bear good fruit is cut down. It is placed in the fire.
You can tell about every tree from its fruit.
Not everyone who says to me 'Lord, Lord' will enter the kingdom of heaven. Only those who do the will of my Father in heaven will enter.
Many will say to me on that day, 'Lord, Lord, did we not prophesy in your name? Did we not cast out demons in your name? Did we not do many miracles in your name?'
From then on, I will tell them very clearly: 'I didn't know you. Go away from me, you are the ones doing evil!' The wise and stupid girls.
Therefore, whoever hears my words and acts on them will be like a wise man who built his house on the rock.
The rain is falling. The water is rising. The winds are blowing and beating against that house. But it is not falling. It is built on the rock.
But everyone who heard my words and did not do them is like a foolish man who built his house on the sand.
The rain falls. The water rises. The wind blows and beats against that house. And oh, a high fall."
Jesus then said all these things. The crowds were amazed at his teaching.
He taught as if he had authority. He didn't speak like the professors of Sharia.
Jesus heals a man who was afflicted with skin disease.
Jesus came down from the mountain. A large crowd followed him.
A man who was afflicted with a skin disease came and knelt down before Jesus. He said, "Lord, if you are willing, you can make me clean."
Jesus stretched out his hand and touched the man. He said, "I am willing to do it. Be clean." Immediately the man was healed of his skin disease.
Then Jesus said to him, "Do not tell anyone, but go and show yourself to the priest and offer the gift that Moses commanded. This will be a testimony to them." A Roman leader who believed.
When Jesus entered Capernaum, a Roman centurion came to him. He asked Jesus for help.
"My Lord," He said, "my servant is beaten in his home and cannot move. He is suffering greatly."
Jesus said: "This is why I walk, so that you may be healed."
The captain answered, "Sir, I am not worthy to have you come under my roof. But just say the word, and my servant will be healed.
I myself am a man under authority. And I have soldiers who obey my orders. I say to this one "Go" and he goes. I say to this one "Come" and he comes. I say to my servant "Do this" and he does it.
When Jesus heard this, he was amazed. He said to his disciples, "I tell you the truth, I have not found anyone in Israel with such great faith.
Let you know that many attacked from the east and the west. They are taking their seats at the feast in the Kingdom of Heaven. They will sit down with Abraham and Isaac and Jacob.
But those who think they are coming from the kingdom will be thrown out, into the darkness. There they will weep and grind their teeth.
Then Jesus said to the Roman centurion, "Go! It will be as you have believed it would happen." And his servant was healed at that very hour. Jesus heals many people.
